B3  the Hardy inequality on the slices
  B3a phi = r^(-a-1-eta): ratio = 1/(a + 1 + eta)^2 -> (a + 1)^-2 (the constant is sharp): pass (a + eta + 1)**(-2)
  B3b the integration by parts behind it: d/dr (r^(2a+2) f^2/(2a+2)) = r^(2a+1) f^2 + r^(2a+2) f f'/(a+1); the boundary
        term at the inner edge enters as -R^(2a+2) f(R)^2/(2a+2) <= 0: pass
